    "estimand": "The within-unit average difference in points per possession (PPP) on PULL_UP possessions occurring after a PNR failure window (`lift`), compared to the unit's baseline PULL_UP PPP. A 'PNR failure' is defined as a game in which the offense's H1 PNR PPP falls below the 20th percentile of its own season distribution AND the team runs at least 5 PNR possessions in each half. Units are offensively-defined team-seasons. The primary metrics are: (i) the proportion of units with positive lift (`prop_pos`) and (ii) the median lift across units (`med_lift`).",
